## Transitive Review

The npm lock contains permissive licenses plus weak-copyleft runtime packages used by Sharp/libvips and Prisma tooling. Upstream package license files are retained in the production dependency tree. The only missing npm SPDX metadata was `seq-queue@0.0.5`; its installed `LICENSE` file is the MIT License. No dependency was modified or statically incorporated into Pizza Logs source.

Re-run this inventory whenever a direct dependency manifest changes. Dependency metadata is evidence, not legal advice.
